Hi, I'm trying to set up CAN1 to listen for **only** CAN ID 0x689. I set the filter up like this but I see other CAN IDs are getting through as well.

twai_filter_config_t f_config = {.acceptance_code = 0x68900000, .acceptance_mask = 0xFF700000, .single_filter = true};

Could someone help to get the correct filter settings for CAN ID 0x689?  Thanks

that's right. I'm on CAN1 with the TWAI interface. Reading 927 msg/s was no problem when the task was running alone on its pinned core. Once I put the GPS task on the same core, I had to bump the TWAI RX queue size a little:

```c++
  twai_general_config_t g_config = TWAI_GENERAL_CONFIG_DEFAULT((gpio_num_t)CAN1_TX, (gpio_num_t)CAN1_RX, TWAI_MODE_LISTEN_ONLY /*TWAI_MODE_NORMAL*/);
  // The E85 CAN bus transmits about 927 messages per second. With a slightly
  // longer rx queue, we observed no queue overruns.
  g_config.rx_queue_len = 16;
```

Merged!

